    {
      "filename": "A rubberized squid- yes, that was a live squid once! (20564597380).jpg",
      "title": "File:A rubberized squid- yes, that was a live squid once! (20564597380).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/58/A_rubberized_squid-_yes%2C_that_was_a_live_squid_once%21_%2820564597380%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_rubberized_squid-_yes,_that_was_a_live_squid_once!_(20564597380).jpg",
      "width": 4288,
      "height": 2848,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "From rubber dinosaur models to rubberized real creatures. Yes, that was once a live squid swimming in the seas near you. After death, silicone was injected into the creature's body to rubberize it and to preserve all it's natural muscles and fibres. This concept was tried with human bodies initially, where an exhibition in China caused much uproar in 1995. People soon got over it, and rubberized real human exhibits are quite common nowadays. Mercifully we didn't see any rubberized human bodies, barring a human heart and a brain (we were encouraged to hold the heart in our hand!), but in this section we saw several siliconized animals. More notes in subsequent captions. (Ottawa, Canada, June 2015)",
      "dateCreated": "2015-06-01 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "canadian-museum-of-nature-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "f244",
      "mediumPath": "_m/f/2/4/4/canadian-museum-of-nature-wp/a-rubberized-squid-yes-that-wa-medium.jpg",
      "smallPath": "_m/f/2/4/4/canadian-museum-of-nature-wp/a-rubberized-squid-yes-that-wa-small.jpg"
    },
    {
      "filename": "A far shot of the real rubberized squid (20759502761).jpg",
      "title": "File:A far shot of the real rubberized squid (20759502761).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/A_far_shot_of_the_real_rubberized_squid_%2820759502761%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_far_shot_of_the_real_rubberized_squid_(20759502761).jpg",
      "width": 4288,
      "height": 2848,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
